  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe Library → Instructions page reports that Devin has no user-wide instructions file. However, Devin CLI supports `AGENTS.md` in its user configuration directory. Magpie's Devin library target appears to be missing the corresponding `Instructions` path.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Magpie: `0.1.1307`\n- Build commit: `efd1b697e401ca9ea771a02720291a0e53ac414b`\n- Devin CLI: `3000.11.92`\n- Platform: macOS, Apple Silicon\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nDevin is detected and appears in Magpie's agent list, but Library → Instructions displays it as having no user-wide instructions file. Shared instructions cannot be enabled for it through the page.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nDevin should be available as a recipient of the Library's shared instructions, written to:\n\n- Linux/macOS: `~/.config/devin/AGENTS.md`\n- Windows: `%APPDATA%\\devin\\AGENTS.md`\n\nThe documentation bundled with Devin CLI 3000.11.92, under **Rules & AGENTS.md → Global Rules**, explicitly documents these locations and states that global rules are loaded at the start of every session. It also supports the singular filename `AGENT.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nIn [`internal/library/targets.go`, lines 302–306](https://github.com/yetone/magpie/blob/efd1b697e401ca9ea771a02720291a0e53ac414b/internal/library/targets.go#L302-L306), the `devin` case configures only MCP and Skills:\n\n```go\ncase \"devin\":\n    t.MCP = &mcpFile{Path: filepath.Join(a.Dir, \"mcp_config.json\"), Format: fmtDevin}\n    t.Skills = filepath.Join(a.Dir, \"skills\")\n```\n\n`t.Instructions` remains empty. Consequently:\n\n- The [Instructions page](https://github.com/yetone/magpie/blob/efd1b697e401ca9ea771a02720291a0e53ac414b/internal/gui/assets/plugins/library/client.js#L1209-L1210) categorizes Devin as having no user-wide instructions file.\n- [`syncInstructions`](https://github.com/yetone/magpie/blob/efd1b697e401ca9ea771a02720291a0e53ac414b/internal/library/instructions.go#L230-L233) returns immediately for this target.\n\nThis is a missing target mapping rather than a check for whether the user's `AGENTS.md` already exists. Creating the file alone would not populate the missing target path.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdd the instructions path to the existing Devin target:\n\n```go\ncase \"devin\":\n    t.Instructions = filepath.Join(a.Dir, \"AGENTS.md\")\n    t.MCP = &mcpFile{Path: filepath.Join(a.Dir, \"mcp_config.json\"), Format: fmtDevin}\n    t.Skills = filepath.Join(a.Dir, \"skills\")\n```\n\n`a.Dir` is already set to Devin's user configuration directory by the [Devin agent adapter](https://github.com/yetone/magpie/blob/efd1b697e401ca9ea771a02720291a0e53ac414b/internal/agent/devin.go#L24-L35), including the Windows location.\n\nSuggested regression coverage:\n\n- The Devin target exposes an `AGENTS.md` instructions path even before the file exists.\n- Enabling shared instructions writes Magpie's managed block to that file while preserving user-authored content outside the block.\n- Devin is offered as an instructions recipient rather than listed as unsupported.",
